id: pm-starter-4kvb
title: Measure agent task cost baselines for extension authors
description: "Reproducible consumer-example baselines for orientation, targeted-read and resume scenarios. Measures tool calls, delivered bytes and elapsed work. Not model performance, not external capture accounting, and not native operation benchmarks."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: audit-1026,cost-baseline
created_at: "2026-10-27T16:56:48.970Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T18:16:47.523Z"
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: Every baseline declares corpus/version and expected answer; repeated runs report distributions; byte/4 estimates are labeled estimates; a deliberate extra full-list call worsens the measured call/byte budget.
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T16:57:06.330Z",pi-agent,"Overlap check (re-run against the pinned SDK 2026.10.23 and sibling package READMEs before design):\n\n- pm-cli ships an internal release ratchet (docs/agent-task-token-baseline.json plus the agent-task token gate). It replays fixed CLI transcripts and compares ceil(bytes/4) estimates for core protocols. That gate is a core release claim, not a consumer example extension authors can run against their own tracker.\n- pm-observer measures external producer captures (transcript tokens, attribution, continuity). It does not measure SDK tool-call and delivered-byte budgets for fixed orientation, targeted-read and resume scenarios.\n- pm-rust benchmarks native workspace operations. It is not a TypeScript consumer example.\n\nThis item is a reproducible pm-starter example for extension authors. It declares corpus/version and an expected answer, reports distributions over repeated runs, labels byte/4 figures as estimates, and shows that one extra full-list call worsens the measured call and byte budget. It does not claim model performance.\n\nDesign: host-injected SDK only (context orient intent, certified list, get, producer cursors, schemaList roles, workspace transactions). No argv/which/symlink SDK resolution."
  "2026-10-27T17:36:51.493Z",codex-agent,"Continuation audit: the prior work is uncommitted on the requested branch; no remote feature branch or open PR exists. Reusing this item and its acceptance criteria. Rechecked sibling scope: observer owns external capture attribution; rust owns native-operation benchmarks; the CLI internal task-token ratchet owns its core release protocol. This package supplies a reproducible consumer example. Preserve the read-only scenario measurement, exact budget comparisons and host injection. The speculative baseline-sync mutation surface is not part of the requested task: it currently splits preview/apply decisions, does not use its transaction hook, and cannot prove deletion ownership. Remove that unsafe unshipped surface; baseline declarations are portable JSON values, with no tracker import, sync, journal, lease or compensation path. Test producer/validator round trips and seeded read-back scenarios instead."
  "2026-10-27T17:54:00.500Z",codex-agent,"Targeted SDK evidence: strict schema and numeric-output fuzzing, 500 seeded portable-declaration replay sequences with periodic native SDK read-back, custom registry role checks, real compact continuation pages, eight-page refusal, corpus revision rechecks, exact rational budget boundaries, and native read-contract fault injection. These are read-only declarations: no package import/export/sync mutation paths or shared journal/lease state exist. Found and corrected SDK short-ID resolution and compact continuation-envelope assumptions. Added a packaged CLI integration test after the harness missed Commander camelCase flag keys. Public read-only copy at main revision bef8690 contains 83 items; initial scenario medians are 2/2/3 calls and 5613/1643/6329 UTF-8 JSON bytes, with an extra full-list delta of 1 call and 290014 bytes. Final runtime and packed-install evidence follows."
  "2026-10-27T18:04:25.448Z",codex-agent,"Verified through the linked pm test runner: 10 tests passed, 0 failed, with 100% lines/branches/functions for baselines.ts at unchanged 100% thresholds. Behavioral revert proof ran in a disposable copy: disabling only executeOnce's injected measured listAllComplete call made the regression fail with budget_not_worsened (exit 1); the actual source hash stayed unchanged and the restored implementation passed the full targeted command. Typecheck, test typecheck and docstring gate pass (102 documented declarations). Public read-only data validation passes on Node 24.19.0 and Bun 1.3.5 with identical answers/byte budgets and unchanged hashes. Two corpus observations cost 2 calls / 580028 bytes separately from the scenario budgets. One writable-fixture run truthfully refused a changed orientation answer; the diagnostic trace is retained in the test and the subsequent exact-source linked run passes. No model/network-remote performance claim is made."
  "2026-10-27T18:06:31.018Z",codex-agent,"Packed acceptance passed all 5 installation paths using the same package bytes (SHA-256 d01c0e3fb1234ebdc0cdff0260eca231bee083fe3639b37af45c205e24813823): npm global, Bun global, npx, bunx forced to Bun, and project-local. Every path replayed the same three answers, passed the full-list budget probe, and returned a typed exit-2 refusal for an invalid repeat count. Runtime identities were Node 24.19.0 and Bun 1.3.5. Local strict tracker health verifies history/storage integrity but reports an ambient pm-github extension-host skew (pinned host 2026.10.23 versus extension 2026.10.27); dependency pins are retained per task rules, and the clean CI health plus npm/Bun release gates will be the authoritative full-gate evidence in the PR. Public tracker version: digest:92fe4c9f9b66e74f154f9b3d7b8032cd035b02699906e29c04518352b4102034. All 83 public items were copied read-only outside git; both runtime validations preserve every file hash. No pm SDK defect is established by the transient orientation refusal: mismatched native focus answers fail safely and are not counted as passing samples."
  "2026-10-27T18:16:44.187Z",codex-agent,"Ready PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-starter/pull/167 (current checks: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-starter/pull/167/checks). Before final-head CI verification, added the missing registration regression that asserts starter baseline suppresses migration writes during preflight. Targeted registration/preflight selection passes 4 tests; the linked preflight selection passes 3 tests. Removing only the baseline preflight condition in a disposable copy fails the new test (true versus false); the actual source hash is unchanged and the fixed test passes after the revert probe. Initial queued CI run 40557212069 is superseded/canceled and is not approval evidence; fresh final-head npm/Bun gate URLs and counts are recorded in the PR. Automated review is unavailable: Greptile trial ended, CodeRabbit skips automatic review, Sourcery exceeds the diff-size limit. No review approval is claimed."
